+ * So the clock is driven from software: whoever runs (the idle loop, a boot-time probe) polls the
+ * counter and pends a group-1 SPI, which is delivered. That takes the place of the timer interrupt:
+ * rtclock_intr() runs and the sleepers of assert_wait_deadline() wake.
